# Infisical Configuration File
# ================================
#
# This file configures the Infisical URL for API-based secret pulling.
# Use this if you're running a self-hosted Infisical instance.
#
# IMPORTANT: This is just a template. DO NOT add real URLs if they contain sensitive info!
#
# Setup Methods:
# --------------
#
# Option 1: Auto-generated (Recommended)
#   Run: pnpm secrets:setup:token
#   The wizard will create this file automatically if you select self-hosted
#
# Option 2: Manual Setup
#   1. Copy this file:
#      cp .infisical-config.example .infisical-config
#
#   2. Edit .infisical-config and set your Infisical URL:
#      INFISICAL_API_URL="https://infisical.yourcompany.com"
#
#   3. Secure the file:
#      chmod 600 .infisical-config
#
# Configuration:
# --------------

# Infisical API URL (without trailing slash)
# For Cloud (default): https://app.infisical.com
# For Self-hosted: https://infisical.yourcompany.com
INFISICAL_API_URL="https://app.infisical.com"

# Examples for self-hosted:
# INFISICAL_API_URL="https://infisical.yourcompany.com"
# INFISICAL_API_URL="https://secrets.example.com"
# INFISICAL_API_URL="http://localhost:8080"  # For local development

# Notes:
# ------
# - This file is auto-ignored by git (.gitignore configured)
# - The URL should NOT include /api/v3/secrets
# - Just the base URL is needed
# - Scripts will automatically append the API paths
# - Both http:// and https:// are supported
# - Remove trailing slashes from the URL

# Priority Order:
# ---------------
# The scripts look for Infisical URL in this order:
# 1. Environment variable: INFISICAL_API_URL
# 2. This config file: .infisical-config
# 3. Default: https://app.infisical.com (Infisical Cloud)

# Usage:
# ------
# Once configured, simply run:
#   pnpm secrets:api              # Pull dev secrets
#   pnpm secrets:api:staging      # Pull staging secrets
#   pnpm secrets:api:prod         # Pull production secrets
#
# The scripts will automatically use the URL from this file.

# Troubleshooting:
# ----------------
# If you get connection errors:
# - Verify the URL is correct and accessible
# - Check that your Infisical instance is running
# - Ensure no firewall is blocking the connection
# - Try accessing the URL in a browser
# - Check if SSL certificate is valid (for https)

# For more information, see:
# - INFISICAL_SETUP.md
# - TOKEN_BASED_SETUP.md
# - scripts/README.md
